msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:103
msgid "**The three LEDs**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:111
msgid "**Bluetooth, again in one line**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:118
msgid "Same object as in the previous chapter. ``bleSerial.begin()`` makes the module advertise as **SunFounder-C2**; the phone writes into **C304** and everything that arrives can be read with ``bleSerial.read()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:122
msgid "**setup()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:135
msgid "**loop() - one character at a time**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:152
msgid "``while`` instead of ``if`` is deliberate: several characters may arrive between two passes of the loop, and this way none of them is left in the buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:155
msgid "The quotes matter - ``'R'`` is the letter R, ``\"R\"`` would be a text of one character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:157
msgid "**toggleLights()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/09-iot_Bluetooth_traffic_light.rst:169
msgid "All three are switched off first, then the wanted one is switched on. That is what keeps a traffic light believable: only one lamp is ever lit."
msgstr ""
